@startuml ideator-state-machine
top to bottom direction
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam state {
 BackgroundColor #F0F6FC
 BorderColor #356282
 ArrowColor #356282
}
hide empty description
title Ideator | problem-solving lifecycle\nDesigned UML state machine — current saved setup; runtime behavior not verified

[*] --> Ready
state "Ready for problem" as Ready
Ready : No problem: introduce workflow and ask
Ready --> Run : problem + optional knobs

state "Active run — persist each phase and decision" as Run {
 state "1. Discover / 2. Define\nProblem diamond" as Problem {
  [*] -down-> Research
  state "Discover: diverge" as Research
  Research : Fresh market-focused research
  Research : Consult sources-knob distinct sources
  Research : Challenges + sticky notes cite evidence
  Research : Label unsourced claims as hypotheses
  Research -down-> RankChallenges
  state "Define: converge" as RankChallenges
  RankChallenges : Score = possible + exciting (1–5 each)
  RankChallenges : Rank; propose at most 5 challenges
  RankChallenges -down-> ChallengeGate
  state ChallengeGate <<choice>>
  ChallengeGate -down-> WaitChallenges : [ask]
  state "Wait for challenge choices" as WaitChallenges #FFF2CC
  WaitChallenges -down-> [*] : user selects / steers
  ChallengeGate -down-> AutoChallenges : [auto]
  state "Auto-select top 5" as AutoChallenges
  AutoChallenges : Ties: exciting, then possible
  AutoChallenges : Record selections and reasons
  AutoChallenges -down-> [*]
 }
 state "3. Develop / 4. Deliver\nSolution diamond" as Solution {
  [*] -down-> Generate
  state "Develop: diverge" as Generate
  Generate : Ideas-knob ideas per picked challenge
  Generate : Fit market culture, habits and rules
  Generate -down-> RankIdeas
  state "Deliver: converge" as RankIdeas
  RankIdeas : Cheap + simple; evidence and uniqueness weights
  RankIdeas : Rank ideas; select at most 5; explain picks
  RankIdeas : Combine ideas into concepts
  RankIdeas -down-> ConceptGate
  state ConceptGate <<choice>>
  ConceptGate -down-> WaitConcepts : [ask]
  state "Wait for concept choices" as WaitConcepts #FFF2CC
  WaitConcepts -down-> [*] : user approves concepts
  ConceptGate -down-> AutoConcepts : [auto]
  state "Auto-select top 2 concepts" as AutoConcepts
  AutoConcepts : Rank by mean constituent weighted score
  AutoConcepts : Ties: mean evidence, then more ideas
  AutoConcepts -down-> [*]
 }
 state "5. Pretotypes / output\nPrepare tests, not tested ideas" as Testing {
  [*] -down-> Design
  state "Design tests + materials" as Design
  Design : Pretotypes-knob total; best concept first
  Design : Hypothesis + success number + deadline
  Design : Explicit go / no-go; first test per concept
  Design : Draft materials only; people run tests
  Design -down-> TestGate
  state TestGate <<choice>>
  TestGate -down-> WaitTests : [ask]
  state "Wait for test selection / start" as WaitTests #FFF2CC
  WaitTests -down-> PrepareDelivery : user answers
  TestGate -down-> PrepareDelivery : [auto] / select recommended first tests
  state "Prepare final outputs" as PrepareDelivery
  PrepareDelivery : Start known: schedule deadline + 1 day
  PrepareDelivery : Else defer check-in until start supplied
  PrepareDelivery : Reports + key results + PNG board
  PrepareDelivery : Shared title across all outputs
  PrepareDelivery -down-> [*] : deliver PNG + requested report(s)
 }
 [*] --> Problem
 Problem -right-> Solution : challenges chosen
 Solution -right-> Testing : concepts chosen
 Testing --> [*]
}

Run --> Delivered : run complete
state "Delivered / awaiting real-world evidence" as Delivered
Delivered : Humans execute selected pretotypes
Delivered : If start missing, wait for start date
Delivered --> Delivered : start provided / schedule deadline + 1 day
Delivered --> Results : scheduled check-in fires / ask for results
state "Await test results" as Results #FFF2CC
Results --> Evaluate : observed results received
state "Evaluate test outcome" as Evaluate
Evaluate : Compare observations with success number
Evaluate : Recommend go, no-go, or iterate
Evaluate : Record in all reports; refresh results and board
Evaluate : Delete spent check-in
Evaluate --> Delivered : outcome recorded; other tests may remain

Run --> Cancelled : user cancels
Delivered --> Cancelled : user cancels run
Results --> Cancelled : user cancels run
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled #FCE4D6
Cancelled : Stop work; mark reports CANCELLED
Cancelled : Delete run check-ins
Cancelled --> [*]

legend bottom
<b>Scoring</b> Weighted idea score = (cheap + simple) × evidence × uniqueness, rounded to 1 decimal.
Cheap / simple: 1–5. Evidence: strong 1.3, some 1.15, none 1.0; cited IDs required.
Uniqueness: non-obvious 1.2, somewhat 1.1, obvious 1.0.
Idea ties: evidence > uniqueness > simple > cheap; then ID order marked unresolved / arbitrary.
<b>Controls</b> Defaults: ideas 5, pretotypes 4, sources 5, country US fallback, language message / English,
format markdown (or page / both), mode auto. Only explicitly chosen mode persists.
Yellow states wait for the user. Auto never pauses during generation. Test execution is external.
Iteration is a recommendation; the setup defines no automatic new ideation / retesting transition.
endlegend
@enduml
